cs/provider_information_mass.md",
    '''# Provider-owned correlation-group information mass

Prob4D can export `group_composite_weight` as a final per-row generalized-Bayes
likelihood power. For a correlation group with `n_g` rows and provider-declared
effective count `m_g`, every row receives `m_g / n_g`. Summing the row powers
therefore recovers `m_g`.

Bayesian-PhysTwin recognizes this contract only through the explicit versioned
metadata value

```text
provider-final-per-row-information-weight-v1
```

When the provider also declares `provider_owns_effective_sample_cap=true`, both
the standard and prior-aware gauge solvers use the supplied row power directly.
They continue to multiply by source reliability and nominal-component evidence,
but do not apply a second row-count cap. Legacy and provider-neutral batches
retain the existing consumer-side effective-sample cap.

This distinction makes the update invariant to duplicating dependent rows while
preserving backward compatibility. Unknown provider-owned semantics fail closed.
The observation adapter records the normalized ownership decision in its batch
metadata and summary so posterior lineage remains auditable.
''',
)
